Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 19:35:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 003/143] dts: opi4a: add a static 2GB /memory node (U-Boot BSP
 does not fill it in)

The vendor U-Boot (v2018.05-t527) shipped on the board does not fill in
/memory in the FDT: it expects a DTB that already carries a static
memory node, like the vendor one. The mainline DTB left it empty, so the
kernel booted with no RAM and hung silently before the first heartbeat.

Describe the 2GB of DRAM fitted to this board at 0x40000000.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 .../boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts  | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index f7e460947..0d6318564 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -22,6 +22,19 @@ chosen {
 		stdout-path = "serial0:115200n8";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The vendor U-Boot (v2018.05-t527) does NOT fill in /memory (it assumes the DTB
+	 * already carries it, like the vendor one). The mainline DTB left it empty -> the kernel
+	 * boots without knowing where the RAM is -> instant silent hang, no
+	 * heartbeat. Define a static /memory like the vendor DTB: base 0x40000000.
+	 * (On a 2GB board use size 0x80000000 instead of 0x1 0x0.)
+	 */
+	memory@40000000 {
+		device_type = "memory";
+		/* OPi4A 2GB: base 0x40000000, size 0x80000000 (2 GiB) */
+		reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
+	};
+
